module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjectiveSpaceEmbedding

/-!
# The single relation presenting the Rees algebra of a regular pair

Let `A` be a commutative ring and let `x₀, x₁ ∈ A` be two elements such that `x₁, x₀` is a weakly
regular sequence — `x₁` is a nonzerodivisor and `x₀` is a nonzerodivisor modulo `x₁`. Then the
kernel of the polynomial presentation `A[T₀, T₁] ⟶ ⨁ₙ Iⁿ` of `Stacks.Blowup.reesPresentation`,
for any ideal `I` containing `x₀` and `x₁`, is the principal ideal generated by the single
Koszul relation `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁`.

For a regular local ring of dimension two and a minimal generating pair `x₀, x₁` of its maximal
ideal the hypothesis holds, so the blowup of such a ring in its maximal ideal is cut out of the
projective line over the base by one equation of degree one.

## Main results

The elided prefix is `Stacks.Blowup`.

* `ker_eval₂Hom_eq_span_relation`: the kernel of `A[T₀, T₁] ⟶ A[X]`, `Tᵢ ↦ xᵢX`, is
  `(x₁T₀ - x₀T₁)`.
* `ker_reesPresentation_eq_span_relation`: the same for
  `Stacks.Blowup.reesPresentation`, whose composition with the inclusion of the Rees algebra into
  `A[X]` is that evaluation.
* `ker_reesPresentation_maximalIdeal_eq_span_relation`: for a regular local ring of dimension two
  and a minimal generating pair of its maximal ideal, unconditionally.
* `isHomogeneous_relation`: the relation is homogeneous of degree one, which is what makes the
  ideal sheaf it cuts out a twist by one.
* `mem_span_relation_of_X_pow_mul_mem` and `mem_span_relation_of_forall_homogeneous_mul_mem`,
  with `mem_span_relation_maximalIdeal_of_forall_homogeneous_mul_mem` in the local case: **the
  relation ideal is saturated**, which is what has to be fed to
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.saturated_idealOfClosedSubscheme` to identify it
  with the homogeneous ideal of equations of the blowup inside the projective line.

Identifying `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme` of
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpace` with the relation ideal is not done in this file: the ideal
of equations is defined by the vanishing of pulled-back twisted sections, and relating it to the
kernel of the graded presentation is the content of the comparison map of
[Stacks, Tag 01N0] part (3). That comparison is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/QuotientComparison.lean`, and the identification it
yields from the two halves below — the kernel and its saturatedness, both proved here — is
`Stacks.Blowup.idealOfClosedSubscheme_blowUpSpecToProjSpace_maximalIdeal_eq_span_relation` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ProjectiveLineIdealOfEquations.lean`.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.ReesAlgebra.ker_reesPresentationHom` computes the same kernel for the *generic* pair: the
Rees algebra of a polynomial ring `R[σ]` along an ideal generated by variables. It is not
instantiable here, since `A` is not a polynomial ring and `x₀, x₁` are not variables — what
replaces the combinatorics of monomials in the generic proof is the regularity of the sequence,
and the proof below is therefore a different one.

The kernel is computed degree by degree. The presentation sends a homogeneous polynomial of
degree `n` to `Xⁿ` times its value at `x` (`Stacks.Blowup.coe_reesPresentation_apply`), so a
polynomial lies in the kernel exactly when each of its homogeneous components vanishes at `x`;
`isHomogeneous_eq_sum` writes a homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` in two variables as
`∑ᵢ aᵢT₀ⁱT₁ⁿ⁻ⁱ`, and `sum_mem_span_relation_of_sum_eq_zero` is the induction on `n`: the
vanishing `∑ᵢ aᵢx₀ⁱx₁ⁿ⁻ⁱ = 0` forces `x₀ⁿaₙ ∈ (x₁)`, hence `aₙ ∈ (x₁)` because `x₀` is a
nonzerodivisor modulo `x₁`; subtracting the corresponding multiple of the relation kills the
leading term, and what is left is `T₁` times a form of degree `n - 1` which still vanishes at `x`
because `x₁` is a nonzerodivisor.

Saturatedness is read off the same kernel computation rather than from primality of the relation:
`T₀ᴺ` is homogeneous of degree `N`, so a saturation hypothesis applies to it, and the presentation
sends `T₀ᴺ` to `(x₀X)ᴺ`, which is a nonzerodivisor in `A[X]` as soon as `x₀` is one in `A`.

The regular sequence of the local case is supplied by
`IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay`
(Tag 00NQ) at the list `[x₁, x₀]`, which is a minimal generating list of the maximal ideal; the
same theorem at `[x₀, x₁]` gives that `x₀` is a nonzerodivisor.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial RingTheory.Sequence
open scoped Pointwise

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

section Pair

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (x : Fin 2 → A)

/-! ### Binary forms -/

/-- Splitting off the top term of a binary form of degree `n + 1`: the rest is divisible by the
second variable. -/
private theorem sum_succ_eq_mul_add {B : Type*} [CommRing B] (y₀ y₁ : B) (c : ℕ → B) (n : ℕ) :
    ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1 + 1), c i * y₀ ^ i * y₁ ^ (n + 1 - i) =
      y₁ * (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), c i * y₀ ^ i * y₁ ^ (n - i)) +
        c (n + 1) * y₀ ^ (n + 1) := by
  have e : n + 1 - (n + 1) = 0 := by omega
  rw [Finset.sum_range_succ, e, pow_zero, mul_one, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine congrArg (· + _) (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_)
  have e' : n + 1 - i = n - i + 1 := by
    have : i ≤ n := Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_range.mp hi)
    omega
  rw [e', pow_succ]
  ring

/-- Changing the top coefficient of a binary form of degree `n` changes it by a multiple of
`y₀ ^ n`. -/
private theorem sum_eq_sum_add {B : Type*} [CommRing B] (y₀ y₁ : B) (c c' : ℕ → B) (δ : B)
    (n : ℕ) (hlt : ∀ i, i < n → c' i = c i) (htop : c' n = c n + δ) :
    ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), c' i * y₀ ^ i * y₁ ^ (n - i) =
      (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), c i * y₀ ^ i * y₁ ^ (n - i)) + δ * y₀ ^ n := by
  rw [Finset.sum_range_succ, Finset.sum_range_succ,
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by rw [hlt i (Finset.mem_range.mp hi)], htop, Nat.sub_self,
    pow_zero]
  ring

/-- A homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` in two variables is the binary form of degree `n` built
from its coefficients. -/
private theorem isHomogeneous_eq_sum {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A} {n : ℕ}
    (hF : F.IsHomogeneous n) :
    F = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1),
      C (coeff (Finsupp.single 0 i + Finsupp.single 1 (n - i)) F) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n - i) := by
  classical
  have hmon : ∀ (i j : ℕ) (c : A), (C c * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ j : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) =
      monomial (Finsupp.single 0 i + Finsupp.single 1 j) c := fun i j c => by
    rw [X_pow_eq_monomial, X_pow_eq_monomial, C_mul_monomial, monomial_mul]
    simp
  have hdeg : ∀ (i : ℕ), i ≤ n →
      (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 2) i + Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 2) (n - i)).degree = n := by
    intro i hi
    rw [map_add, Finsupp.degree_single, Finsupp.degree_single]
    omega
  refine MvPolynomial.ext _ _ fun d => ?_
  rw [coeff_sum]
  simp only [hmon, coeff_monomial]
  by_cases hd : d.degree = n
  · have hd2 : d 0 + d 1 = n := by
      rw [Finsupp.degree_eq_sum, Fin.sum_univ_two] at hd
      exact hd
    have hde : Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 2) (d 0) + Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 2) (n - d 0) = d := by
      refine Finsupp.ext (Fin.forall_fin_two.mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩)
      · have e0 : (Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 2) (n - d 0)) 0 = 0 :=
          Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (by decide)
        rw [Finsupp.add_apply, e0, Finsupp.single_eq_same, add_zero]
      · have e1 : (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 2) (d 0)) 1 = 0 :=
          Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (by decide)
        rw [Finsupp.add_apply, e1, Finsupp.single_eq_same, zero_add]
        omega
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem (d 0) (Finset.mem_range.mpr (by omega))]
    · rw [hde, if_pos rfl]
    · intro i _ hne
      refine if_neg fun h => hne ?_
      have h0 := congrArg (fun f : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ => f 0) h
      simpa using h0
  · rw [hF.coeff_eq_zero hd]
    refine (Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi => if_neg fun h => hd ?_).symm
    rw [← h]
    exact hdeg i (Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_range.mp hi))

/-! ### The kernel of the presentation -/

/-- The first member of a weakly regular pair is a nonzerodivisor. -/
private theorem nonzerodivisor_of_isWeaklyRegular {y z : A} (h : IsWeaklyRegular A [y, z]) :
    ∀ a : A, y * a = 0 → a = 0 := fun a ha =>
  ((isWeaklyRegular_cons_iff A y [z]).mp h).1
    (show y • a = y • (0 : A) by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using ha)

/-- A property that can be divided by `y` can be divided by any power of `y`. -/
private theorem pow_mul_imp_of_mul_imp {P : A → Prop} {y : A} (h : ∀ a, P (y * a) → P a) :
    ∀ (k : ℕ) (c : A), P (y ^ k * c) → P c := by
  intro k
  induction k with
  | zero => intro c hc; simpa using hc
  | succ k ih =>
    intro c hc
    refine ih c (h _ ?_)
    rwa [← mul_assoc, ← pow_succ']

/-- **The relations of the Rees algebra of a regular pair, degreewise.** A binary form of degree
`n` vanishing at a pair `x₀, x₁` whose reverse is a regular sequence lies in the ideal generated
by `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁`. -/
private theorem sum_mem_span_relation_of_sum_eq_zero
    (h1 : ∀ a : A, x 1 * a = 0 → a = 0)
    (h0 : ∀ a : A, x 0 * a ∈ Ideal.span {x 1} → a ∈ Ideal.span {x 1}) (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ a : ℕ → A, ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), a i * x 0 ^ i * x 1 ^ (n - i) = 0 →
      ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), C (a i) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n - i) ∈
        Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro a ha
    simp only [zero_add, Finset.range_one, Finset.sum_singleton, pow_zero, Nat.sub_self,
      mul_one] at ha ⊢
    rw [ha, map_zero]
    exact Ideal.zero_mem _
  | succ n ih =>
    intro a ha
    classical
    rw [sum_succ_eq_mul_add] at ha
    have hdvd : x 0 ^ (n + 1) * a (n + 1) ∈ Ideal.span {x 1} :=
      Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr
        ⟨-(∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), a i * x 0 ^ i * x 1 ^ (n - i)), by linear_combination -ha⟩
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp
      (pow_mul_imp_of_mul_imp (P := (· ∈ Ideal.span {x 1})) h0 _ _ hdvd)
    obtain ⟨a', hlt, htop⟩ :
        ∃ a' : ℕ → A, (∀ i, i < n → a' i = a i) ∧ a' n = a n + b * x 0 :=
      ⟨fun i => if i = n then a n + b * x 0 else a i, fun i hi => if_neg (by omega), if_pos rfl⟩
    have hS' : ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), a' i * x 0 ^ i * x 1 ^ (n - i) = 0 := by
      refine h1 _ ?_
      rw [sum_eq_sum_add (x 0) (x 1) a a' (b * x 0) n hlt htop]
      linear_combination ha + x 0 ^ (n + 1) * hb
    have hupd : (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), C (a' i) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n - i) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) =
        (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), C (a i) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n - i)) +
          C b * C (x 0) * X 0 ^ n :=
      sum_eq_sum_add (X 0 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) (X 1)
        (fun i => (C (a i) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A))
        (fun i => (C (a' i) : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)) (C b * C (x 0)) n
        (fun i hi => by rw [hlt i hi])
        (by rw [htop, map_add, map_mul])
    have key : (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1 + 1), C (a i) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n + 1 - i) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) =
        X 1 * (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), C (a' i) * X 0 ^ i * X 1 ^ (n - i)) +
          C b * X 0 ^ n * (C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1) := by
      rw [sum_succ_eq_mul_add, hupd, ← hb, map_mul]
      ring
    rw [key]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (ih a' hS'))
      (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _))

/-- The presentation sends a homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` to `Xⁿ` times its value at
`x`. -/
private theorem eval₂Hom_eq_monomial {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A} {n : ℕ}
    (hF : F.IsHomogeneous n) :
    MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (Polynomial.C : A →+* Polynomial A)
        (fun i => Polynomial.C (x i) * Polynomial.X) F =
      Polynomial.monomial n (MvPolynomial.eval x F) := by
  have hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range x) := fun i => Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  rw [← coe_reesPresentation_apply (Ideal.span (Set.range x)) x hx hF]
  exact (DFunLike.congr_fun
    (val_comp_reesPresentation (Ideal.span (Set.range x)) x hx) F).symm

/-- **The kernel of the Rees presentation of a regular pair is the single Koszul relation.** For
`x₀, x₁` in a commutative ring such that `x₁, x₀` is a weakly regular sequence, a polynomial
`F ∈ A[T₀, T₁]` with `F(x₀X, x₁X) = 0` in `A[X]` is a multiple of `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁`. -/
theorem ker_eval₂Hom_eq_span_relation (hreg : IsWeaklyRegular A [x 1, x 0]) :
    RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (Polynomial.C : A →+* Polynomial A)
        (fun i => Polynomial.C (x i) * Polynomial.X)) =
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} := by
  obtain ⟨-, hr0⟩ := (isWeaklyRegular_cons_iff A (x 1) [x 0]).mp hreg
  have hsub : (x 1 • (⊤ : Submodule A A) : Submodule A A) = Ideal.span {x 1} := by
    rw [← Submodule.ideal_span_singleton_smul, Ideal.smul_eq_mul, Ideal.mul_top]
  have h1 : ∀ a : A, x 1 * a = 0 → a = 0 := nonzerodivisor_of_isWeaklyRegular hreg
  have h0 : ∀ a : A, x 0 * a ∈ Ideal.span {x 1} → a ∈ Ideal.span {x 1} := by
    have hr0' := (isWeaklyRegular_singleton_iff (QuotSMulTop (x 1) A) (x 0)).mp hr0
    intro a ha
    have hz : (x 0) • (Submodule.Quotient.mk a : QuotSMulTop (x 1) A) =
        (x 0) • (0 : QuotSMulTop (x 1) A) := by
      rw [smul_zero, ← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
      rw [hsub, smul_eq_mul]
      exact ha
    have := hr0' hz
    rw [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, hsub] at this
    exact this
  refine le_antisymm (fun F hF => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at hF
    have hcomp : ∀ k, MvPolynomial.eval x (homogeneousComponent k F) = 0 := by
      have hpsi : ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (F.totalDegree + 1),
          Polynomial.monomial k (MvPolynomial.eval x (homogeneousComponent k F)) = 0 := by
        rw [← hF]
        conv_rhs => rw [← MvPolynomial.sum_homogeneousComponent F]
        rw [map_sum]
        exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ =>
          (eval₂Hom_eq_monomial x (homogeneousComponent_isHomogeneous k F)).symm
      intro k
      by_cases hk : k < F.totalDegree + 1
      · have h := congrArg (fun p : Polynomial A => p.coeff k) hpsi
        simp only [Polynomial.finsetSum_coeff, Polynomial.coeff_monomial,
          Polynomial.coeff_zero] at h
        rwa [Finset.sum_ite_eq' (Finset.range (F.totalDegree + 1)) k
          (fun k => MvPolynomial.eval x (homogeneousComponent k F)),
          if_pos (Finset.mem_range.mpr hk)] at h
      · rw [homogeneousComponent_eq_zero k F (by omega), map_zero]
    rw [← MvPolynomial.sum_homogeneousComponent F]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun k _ => ?_
    rw [isHomogeneous_eq_sum (homogeneousComponent_isHomogeneous k F)]
    refine sum_mem_span_relation_of_sum_eq_zero x h1 h0 k _ ?_
    have h := hcomp k
    rw [isHomogeneous_eq_sum (homogeneousComponent_isHomogeneous k F)] at h
    simpa using h
  · intro p hp
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hp
    subst hp
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, map_mul, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C,
      MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X']
    ring

/-- **The kernel of the polynomial presentation of the Rees algebra of a regular pair.** For
`x₀, x₁` elements of an ideal `I` such that `x₁, x₀` is a weakly regular sequence, the kernel of
`Stacks.Blowup.reesPresentation` is generated by the single relation `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁`. -/
theorem ker_reesPresentation_eq_span_relation (I : Ideal A) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hreg : IsWeaklyRegular A [x 1, x 0]) :
    RingHom.ker (reesPresentation I x hx).toRingHom =
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} := by
  rw [← ker_eval₂Hom_eq_span_relation x hreg, ← val_comp_reesPresentation I x hx,
    RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _ (fun p q h => Subtype.ext h)]

/-- The relation `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁` is homogeneous of degree one. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_relation :
    (C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A).IsHomogeneous 1 :=
  ((isHomogeneous_C_mul_X (x 1) 0).sub (isHomogeneous_C_mul_X (x 0) 1))

/-! ### Saturation -/

/-- **A power of `T₀` may be divided out of the relation ideal.** If `x₀` is a nonzerodivisor,
`T₀ⁿF ∈ (x₁T₀ - x₀T₁)` forces `F ∈ (x₁T₀ - x₀T₁)`. -/
theorem mem_span_relation_of_X_pow_mul_mem (hreg : IsWeaklyRegular A [x 1, x 0])
    (hx0 : ∀ a : A, x 0 * a = 0 → a = 0) {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A} {N : ℕ}
    (h : (X 0 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) ^ N * F ∈
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)}) :
    F ∈ Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} := by
  rw [← ker_eval₂Hom_eq_span_relation x hreg, RingHom.mem_ker] at h ⊢
  rw [map_mul, map_pow, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X'] at h
  refine Polynomial.ext fun k => ?_
  rw [Polynomial.coeff_zero]
  refine pow_mul_imp_of_mul_imp (P := (· = 0)) hx0 N _ ?_
  have hk := congrArg (fun p : Polynomial A => p.coeff (k + N)) h
  simp only [mul_pow, ← Polynomial.C_pow, mul_assoc, Polynomial.coeff_C_mul,
    Polynomial.coeff_X_pow_mul, Polynomial.coeff_zero] at hk
  exact hk

/-- **The relation ideal is saturated.** If every homogeneous element of some degree `N`
multiplies `F` into `(x₁T₀ - x₀T₁)`, then `F` itself lies in it. This is the hypothesis
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.saturated_idealOfClosedSubscheme` asks for, read at
the relation ideal. -/
theorem mem_span_relation_of_forall_homogeneous_mul_mem (hreg : IsWeaklyRegular A [x 1, x 0])
    (hx0 : ∀ a : A, x 0 * a = 0 → a = 0) {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A} {N : ℕ}
    (h : ∀ y ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) A N, y * F ∈
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)}) :
    F ∈ Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} :=
  mem_span_relation_of_X_pow_mul_mem x hreg hx0
    (h _ ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule N _).mpr (isHomogeneous_X_pow 0 N)))

end Pair

section RegularLocalRing

open IsLocalRing

/-- A minimal generating pair of the maximal ideal of a two-dimensional regular local ring is a
regular sequence, in either order: it is a minimal generating list of `𝔪`, so [Stacks, Tag 00NQ]
applies to it. -/
private theorem isWeaklyRegular_pair_of_span (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (y z : A) (hyz : Ideal.span {y, z} = maximalIdeal A) :
    IsWeaklyRegular A [y, z] := by
  have hfr : (maximalIdeal A).spanFinrank = 2 := by
    have h := IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := A)
    rw [hdim] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hlist : Ideal.ofList [y, z] = maximalIdeal A := by
    have h : {r : A | r ∈ [y, z]} = {y, z} := by ext r; simp
    rw [Ideal.ofList, h, hyz]
  exact (((IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
    A).1 [y, z] hlist (by simp [hfr])).1).toIsWeaklyRegular

/-- A minimal generating pair of the maximal ideal spans it as a pair. -/
private theorem span_pair_eq_maximalIdeal {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (x : Fin 2 → A) (hspan : maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    Ideal.span {x 0, x 1} = maximalIdeal A := by
  have hrange : Set.range x = {x 0, x 1} := by
    ext y
    simp [Fin.exists_fin_two, eq_comm]
  rw [hspan, hrange]

/-- The reversed minimal generating pair `x₁, x₀` of the maximal ideal is weakly regular. -/
private theorem isWeaklyRegular_swap_pair_of_span (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (x : Fin 2 → A)
    (hspan : maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) : IsWeaklyRegular A [x 1, x 0] :=
  isWeaklyRegular_pair_of_span A hdim (x 1) (x 0)
    (by rw [Set.pair_comm (x 1) (x 0)]; exact span_pair_eq_maximalIdeal x hspan)

/-- **The blowup of a regular local surface is cut out of the projective line by one equation of
degree one.** For `A` a regular local ring of dimension two and `x₀, x₁` a minimal generating pair
of its maximal ideal, the kernel of the polynomial presentation of the Rees algebra of `𝔪` is
generated by `x₁T₀ - x₀T₁`. -/
theorem ker_reesPresentation_maximalIdeal_eq_span_relation (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (x : Fin 2 → A)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ maximalIdeal A) (hspan : maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    RingHom.ker (reesPresentation (maximalIdeal A) x hx).toRingHom =
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} :=
  ker_reesPresentation_eq_span_relation x (maximalIdeal A) hx
    (isWeaklyRegular_swap_pair_of_span A hdim x hspan)

/-- **The relation ideal of a regular local surface is saturated.** -/
theorem mem_span_relation_maximalIdeal_of_forall_homogeneous_mul_mem (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (x : Fin 2 → A)
    (hspan : maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) {F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A} {N : ℕ}
    (h : ∀ y ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) A N, y * F ∈
      Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)}) :
    F ∈ Ideal.span {(C (x 1) * X 0 - C (x 0) * X 1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A)} :=
  mem_span_relation_of_forall_homogeneous_mul_mem x
    (isWeaklyRegular_swap_pair_of_span A hdim x hspan)
    (nonzerodivisor_of_isWeaklyRegular
      (isWeaklyRegular_pair_of_span A hdim (x 0) (x 1) (span_pair_eq_maximalIdeal x hspan))) h

end RegularLocalRing

end Stacks.Blowup

